From: SWEET RMX1971 port (ZCode agent + AppleCampus)
Subject: [PATCH 0085] sweet: DWC3 DMA diagnostics

The 2026-10-27 boot produced the sweet_usb_probe() register dump but not a
single line from sweet_usb_gadget_start(): no "soft reset", no "no DMA
memory", no "endpoint 0 setup failed" anywhere in the 4 MiB console log,
while the volume-key driver (same patch, same boot) logged normally. The
only silent exit in that function is pmap_find_phys() returning 0, so print
the allocation address and the translation result before deciding whether
the DMA area or the pmap lookup is at fault.
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -861,12 +861,17 @@
 	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &ud.dma, UD_SIZE, PAGE_MASK, 0, 0,
 	    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO | KMA_PERMANENT, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
-		printf("SWEET USB: no DMA memory\n");
+		printf("SWEET USB: no DMA memory (%u bytes)\n", (unsigned)UD_SIZE);
 		return;
 	}
+	printf("SWEET USB: dma va=%#llx size=%#x\n",
+	    (unsigned long long)ud.dma, (unsigned)UD_SIZE);
 	ppnum_t pn = pmap_find_phys(kernel_pmap, (addr64_t)ud.dma);
 	if (!pn) {
+		printf("SWEET USB: pmap_find_phys(va=%#llx) returned 0\n",
+		    (unsigned long long)ud.dma);
 		return;
 	}
+	printf("SWEET USB: dma pa=%#llx\n", (unsigned long long)ptoa_64(pn));
 	ud.dma_pa = ptoa_64(pn);
 	ud_if_create();
 
